Z||000000||anthony_86gt||03-07-2001||04:16 PM||||I replaced my distributor cap and rotor on my 86 gt.  Now my car wont start?? whats wrong? and when i was disconnecting my battery the wrench touched + and - and and you know what that does.  did i blow a fuse?  but i really need help bad. i also replaced the plugs and made sure the firing order was right.  thanks a lot please help me i want my car to work!!<P>the distributor is also very rusty.||||reg||5
Z||000001||daved||03-07-2001||10:36 PM||||Tony, Try one of those old plugs on any wire and tell us if you get a spark at all.  You need to narrow it down some.<BR>A spark would mean you put the plug wires on wrong (started at the incorrect place on the Dist.?)<BR>If no spark, then you may have damaged something.  Let us know,  Dave||||reg||1
Z||000002||anthony_86gt||03-08-2001||02:51 PM||||yes i am getting spark.  but i only check a couple of the wires if they had spark,  could it just be 1 wire.  and i smell plenty of gas too. and i have tried the old cap & rotor.||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||03-08-2001||06:46 PM||||For just one wire to be out so it won't start, it pretty much has to be the coil wire.  When you say you have spark, do you mean you're getting spark when you put a plug onto one of the <B>plug</B> wires (and ground the plug's body)?<BR>      ||||reg||1
Z||000004||daved||03-08-2001||10:41 PM||||Try reading the later posts of the "timing by ear" recent thread. <BR>Locate the CORRECT position of #1 compression stroke TDC. Remove the distributor cap and check that the rotor points to the post leading to #1 plug. Re-check from this datum, that you do indeed have all the plug wires in the proper location.  Let us know what you find,  Dave||||reg||1
